            <ArticleTitle>Churg-Strauss syndrome associated with montelukast therapy.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>604-5</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1080/02770900903006273</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Churg-Strauss syndrome is a rare form of eosinophilic vasculitis associated with asthma. Several cases of eosinophilic conditions including Churg-Strauss syndrome have recently been reported in asthmatic patients being treated with antileukotriene receptor antagonists. However, whether these drugs have a direct pathogenic role remains controversial. We describe two patients who developed Churg-Strauss syndrome after starting treatment with montelukast.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
